Solve the following mathematics problem. Show your working and put the final answer in \boxed{...}.

Let \[f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
2x + 7 & \text{if } x < -2, \\
-x^2 - x + 1 & \text{if } x \ge -2.
\end{array}
\right.\]Find the sum of all values of $x$ such that $f(x) = -5.$

Solve the following mathematics problem. Show your working and put the final answer in \boxed{...}.

Let \[f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
\frac{x}{21} & \text{ if }x\text{ is a multiple of 3 and 7}, \\
3x & \text{ if }x\text{ is only a multiple of 7}, \\
7x & \text{ if }x\text{ is only a multiple of 3}, \\
x+3 & \text{ if }x\text{ is not a multiple of 3 or 7}.
\end{array}
\right.\]If $f^a(x)$ means the function is nested $a$ times (for example, $f^2(x)=f(f(x))$), what is the smallest value of $a$ greater than 1 that satisfies $f(2)=f^a(2)$?

Solve the following mathematics problem. Show your working and put the final answer in \boxed{...}.

Let \[f(n) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
n^2-2 & \text{ if }n<0, \\
2n-20 & \text{ if }n \geq 0.
\end{array}
\right.\]What is the positive difference between the two values of $a$ that satisfy the equation $f(-2)+f(2)+f(a)=0$?

Solve the following mathematics problem. Show your working and put the final answer in \boxed{...}.

For real numbers $x$, let \[f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
x+2 &\text{ if }x>3, \\
2x+a &\text{ if }x\le 3.
\end{array}
\right.\]What must the value of $a$ be to make the piecewise function continuous (which means that its graph can be drawn without lifting your pencil from the paper)?

Solve the following mathematics problem. Show your working and put the final answer in \boxed{...}.

Suppose that $x$ is an integer that satisfies the following congruences: \begin{align*}
3+x &\equiv 2^2 \pmod{3^3} \\
5+x &\equiv 3^2 \pmod{5^3} \\
7+x &\equiv 5^2 \pmod{7^3}
\end{align*}What is the remainder when $x$ is divided by $105$?
